## TL;DR – Quick copy-paste snippet (CDN)

```html
<script type="module">
import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';
import { PMTiles } from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@protomaps/pmtiles@latest/dist/pmtiles.mjs';

const pm = new PMTiles('https://example.com/tiles.pmtiles');
maplibregl.addProtocol('pmtiles', (req) => pm.get(req));

const map = new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: { version:8, sources:{}, layers:[] },
  center: [0,0],
  zoom: 2
});

map.on('load', () => {
  map.addSource('my-source', { type:'vector', url:'pmtiles://tiles.pmtiles' });
  map.addLayer({
    id:'my-line',
    type:'line',
    source:'my-source',
    'source-layer':'my_layer_name',
    paint:{ 'line-color':'#ff6600', 'line-width':2 }
  });
});
</script>
```

Replace:

* `https://example.com/tiles.pmtiles` – URL to your PMTiles file (must support HTTP range requests).  
* `my_layer_name` – the exact layer name inside the vector tiles you want to draw.

That’s it! Your PMTiles vector data will now appear as a styled line layer on the MapLibre map. Happy mapping!
